  "note": "Faction reputation (roadmap item 17, first part; core/game/game_factions.gd, checked by tools/check_data.gd). NPCs judge the heir by their ancestors. A faction's standing with the heir (-100 to 100) is worked out, never saved, from what the house remembers: every heir the chronicle still keeps in full (and the living heir, whose own deeds count in full) is weighed by the faction's `remembers` rules, and an ancestor's deeds fade by the faction's `memory` for each generation that has passed; `house` rules weigh what belongs to the whole house (its glory and infamy echoes, the legends it has slain, the milestones it has reached). A rule is {what, each, cap?} with `what` one of: class (the heir's class is in `classes`), level (each full `per` levels), battles (each full `per` won), kills (each full `per` kills of the `creatures` or of creatures with one of `tags`), gold (each full `per` gold held at the end), cause (died of one of `causes`), titles (each personal title). `cap` bounds what one heir can add by a rule, either way. A house rule is {what, each, cap?} with `what` one of: echo (`kind`; each is per 1.0 of strength), bosses (each of `ids` slain), milestones (each reached). Standing gives a rank (`ranks`, lowest first, each from its `min` up). At `boon_rank` or better a faction offers the living heir a gift once in their life, in a town (`boon`: gold scaled by the generation as prices are, potions and XP scaled by the heir's level; `honoured_mult` at the top rank), and at the top rank confers a title (the title's condition is {faction: id}). Nothing is random. The autopilot takes no gift, and no price or fight reads a standing yet. A town with a faction (`towns`) feels that faction's standing with the heir in its prices, hire fees and training (`town_effects`, by rank): shop and temple prices (GameItems.price_mult), companions' hire fees (GameParty.fee) and the XP of training (GameDynasty.train). Outside those towns, and for a faction with no town, every number is as it was. Still no dice.",
